<script>
  import Meta from '../components/Meta.brm';
  import Network from '../components/Network.brm';
  import Shipped from '../components/Shipped.brm';
  import Counter from '../demos/Counter.brm';
  import * as counter from '../demos/Counter.brm?inspect';
  import Todos from '../demos/Todos.brm';
  import * as todos from '../demos/Todos.brm?inspect';

  const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
</script>

#head {
  <title>brumate: web apps that resume</title>
}

<Meta
  title="brumate: web apps that resume"
  description="A component language and compiler. Components render on the server, and the browser loads each handler only when it's needed. No hydration."
  path=""
/>
<main class="home">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <p class="eyebrow">A component language and compiler</p>
    <h1>Web apps that <span class="gradient-text">resume</span>, not hydrate.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Components render on the server. The browser keeps their state and loads each handler
      only when it's needed. Pages work at once, and nothing runs twice.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href=(`${base}docs/getting-started`)>Get started</a>
      <a class="button" href=(`${base}docs`)>Read the docs</a>
    </div>
    <pre class="install"><span class="prompt">$</span> pnpm add brumate</pre>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Try it on this page</h2>
    <p class="section-lead">
      These demos are brumate components, rendered when this page was built. The list on the right shows every script the page has loaded.
      Before you touch a demo, it holds only the loader. Use one and watch its code arrive.
    </p>
    <div class="playground">
      <div class="demos">
        <figure class="demo">
          <figcaption>Counter</figcaption>
          <Counter />
        </figure>
        <figure class="demo">
          <figcaption>Todos</figcaption>
          <Todos />
        </figure>
      </div>
      <Network />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>What the compiler ships</h2>
    <p class="section-lead">
      The compiler builds the graph of what reads what once, when it compiles. Each handler is its own module.
      Markup that cannot change ships as HTML only. These tables come from <code>brumate inspect</code>, run when this site was built.
    </p>
    <div class="showcase">
      <article class="showcase-item">
        <h3>Counter</h3>
        {counter.source}
        <Shipped report=(counter.report) />
      </article>
      <article class="showcase-item">
        <h3>Todos</h3>
        {todos.source}
        <Shipped report=(todos.report) />
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section features">
    <article class="feature">
      <h3>No hydration</h3>
      <p>The server writes state into the page. The browser reads it when an event needs it, and never renders a component again to find it.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature">
      <h3>Code per event</h3>
      <p>Each handler is a module that loads when its event fires, or when the pointer is over its element. Markup that never changes ships no code.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature">
      <h3>Streaming first</h3>
      <p>The first render goes out whole. <code>#loading</code> bodies stream in after it, as their data resolves.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature">
      <h3>Server functions</h3>
      <p>Mark a function with <code>'use server'</code>, and the browser calls it over the network. A form posts to it without any script.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature">
      <h3>Routes and layouts</h3>
      <p>File routes with layouts and sibling routes. Links load pages in place and keep the layouts, with their state.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="feature">
      <h3>Typed</h3>
      <p><code>brumate-tsc</code> checks scripts, markup, props, events, and that every value sent to the browser can be serialized.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta">
    <h2>Start with one component</h2>
    <p>A <code>.brm</code> file, the Vite plugin and a server that streams pages.</p>
    <a class="button primary" href=(`${base}docs/getting-started`)>Get started</a>
  </section>
</main>
